1) 执行 echo ruok | nc \u003chost\u003e 21:
1) Run echo ruok | nc <host> 2181 to reproduce it by hand, then echo srvr | nc <host> 2181 to read Mode and Connections;
2) Check whether the 4lw allowlist (4lw.commands.whitelist in zoo.cfg) is rejecting the probe — that is a false positive, just open the allowlist;
3) For a genuine problem, check the log for JVM full GC or a full disk;
4) Run echo mntr | nc <host> 2181 and check whether zk_outstanding_requests is piling up, which means it can no longer keep up.

1) 登录主机确认进程是否存活（jps 或 systemctl status z:
1) Log in to the host and confirm the process is alive (jps or systemctl status zookeeper);
2) If it is alive, run echo ruok | nc <host> 2181 and see whether it answers imok, to tell a hung process apart from a network problem;
3) If it is not running, check zookeeper.out or the files under logs/ for the exit reason — a full disk and JVM OOM are the most common;
4) After restarting, run echo srvr | nc <host> 2181 to confirm it rejoined the cluster and finished syncing.

1) 逐个节点执行 echo srvr | nc \u003chost\u003:
1) Run echo srvr | nc <host> 2181 on each node and read Mode to confirm whether the number of live nodes has fallen below quorum;
2) If quorum is lost, bring the downed nodes back first — the cluster elects a leader automatically once the majority is restored;
3) If all nodes are alive but no leader is elected, check connectivity on ports 2888/3888 and whether any myid is duplicated;
4) Check the election errors in each node's log — a corrupted transaction log is common, in which case sync a snapshot from another node and restart.

